    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subsequent annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Depression screen negative. Fall risk moderate from frailty, with no falls on bedtime tamsulosin. Advance care planning completed today. [S]<list><item>Next annual wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic urinary retention on a catheter (R33.8)</content>. No infection since March; catheter changes on schedule. [S]<list><item>Second trial without catheter at the review in about five weeks, after four months of finasteride.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Mild frailty (R54)</content>. Timed Up and Go 14 seconds, a little better than 15 in March; weight steady. [S]<list><item>Continue daily walking; a physiotherapist visit for strength and balance exercises.</item><item>Add a protein-rich snack each day.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Respiratory syncytial virus vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Single dose given today; recommended at 75 and older</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today; no further doses needed</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dose 1 given today; dose 2 due in two to six months</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>High-dose vaccine due when the new season&apos;s vaccine arrives in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended at 65 and older on the current schedule; he will have it at the pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis booster</td><td>Due</td><td>No dose on record in the past ten years; to be given with the second zoster dose</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 1</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Referred</td><td>Timed Up and Go 14 seconds; referred to physiotherapy for strength and balance exercises</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Whispered-voice test passed</td></tr><tr><td>Vision</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Eye examination last year</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Mini-Cog 4 in March; normal by observation today</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>A colonoscopy at 72 was normal by his report; at 80, with mild frailty, he and his physician agree that further screening offers little benefit</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not recommended at 70 and older; PSA is followed only as part of his finasteride treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Statin for primary prevention</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Evidence is insufficient at 76 and older; discussed, and he prefers no new daily medicine</td></tr><tr><td>Abdominal aortic aneurysm and lung cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C and diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Hepatitis C screening is recommended to 79; diabetes screening is for overweight adults to 70; glucose has been normal</td></tr><tr><td>Advance care planning</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Health care agent named and his wishes recorded today</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Respiratory syncytial virus vaccine (adjuvanted), single dose; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20; Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: American Geriatrics Society 2023 updated AGS Beers Criteria for potentially inappropriate medication use in older adults (2023); Medicare Wellness Visits (Medicare Learning Network) (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Five-month review with the second trial without catheter in about five weeks. Second zoster dose and the Tdap booster in two to six months. Influenza vaccine in the autumn. Next annual wellness visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 1941-07-14: five-month review with a planned second trial without catheter. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
